1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:13,825
Before shipping containers, cargo was loaded piece by piece, and every port worked differently. A software container packs an app with everything it needs, and runs the same everywhere.

2
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:17,645
Docker builds and runs containers.

3
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:28,600
A Dockerfile is the recipe for a container: start from a base, copy your code, install what it needs, and say how to run it.

4
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:39,400
With many containers, Kubernetes is the harbour master: it places them, restarts failed ones, and adds more when busy.

5
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:44,175
Start simple. Many apps never need Kubernetes.

